@page "/editor/csharp"
@using Playground.Blazor.Components.Pages
@inject NavigationManager Navigation
@* RAZOR_PLAN.md, R3a / R3b: the C# of the page is one virtual C# document — the C# the SDK's generator makes of it (the class of the
   component, `__builder.AddContent(…, <expr>)` for the expressions of the markup, the members of `@code`, `_Imports.razor` of the
   project), injected into the file piece by piece; the plugin's C# works through it.

   TYPE:razor-completion — on the empty line under `<ul>` below type `<li>@cou` and wait for the popup (or Ctrl+Space). EXPECT: `count`
   and `Counter` in the list, `count` first; Enter writes `count`. Then type `.` after it: the members of int (`ToString`, `CompareTo`).
   Ctrl+Z until the line is empty.

   TYPE:razor-goto — Ctrl+B (or Ctrl+click) on `count` in `<p>Count: @count</p>`. EXPECT: the caret goes to `private int count;` in
   `@code` below. Ctrl+B on `Step` in `@(new Counter().Step)`: `Counter.razor`, its `[Parameter] public int Step`. Ctrl+B on
   `Navigation` in `Navigation.Uri`: the `@inject` line of this file.

   TYPE:razor-errors — in `Increase` below `count += 1;` type `count = "x";`. EXPECT: `"x"` red with CS0029 after a moment, as in a
   `.cs` file; Ctrl+Z takes it away. Checked by the robot in WSL (0.1.289; before it, `@code` was silent in a project the generator
   had run for).

   TYPE:razor-code-completion — in `Increase` below `count += 1;` type `var u = Navigation.` EXPECT: the members of NavigationManager
   (`BaseUri`, `Uri`, `NavigateTo`…) first, the postfix templates after; `cou` — `count [int]`; in `@code` outside a method
   `protected override ` — `OnInitialized`, `OnInitializedAsync`, `OnParametersSet`…; `[Para` — `Parameter`; `Coun` — `Counter` of
   Playground.Blazor.Components.Pages and of System.Diagnostics.Metrics only, none of the Broken project, which Blazor does not
   reference (0.1.289; the same in a .cs file of Blazor). Ctrl+Z.

   TYPE:razor-inlay-hints — look at `@Sum(2, 3)` below and at `Twice` in `@code`. EXPECT: the hints of C# as in a `.cs` file (Settings |
   Editor | Inlay Hints | Razor): `left:` `right:` before `2` and `3`, `right:` before `1` in `Sum(count, 1)` (none before `count`: hints of
   other arguments are off by default, as in C#), the type at `var
   total`; none at `@count` of the markup (the generator's `AddContent(…, count)` is not the user's call). *@

<h3>C# in the markup</h3>
<p>Count: @count, at @Navigation.Uri</p>
<p>Step of the counter: @(new Counter().Step)</p>
<p>Sum: @Sum(2, 3)</p>
<ul>

</ul>

@code {
    private int count;

    private void Increase()
    {
        count += 1;
    }

    private int Sum(int left, int right) => left + right;

    private int Twice()
    {
        var total = Sum(count, 1);
        return total * 2;
    }
}
